From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:18:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AOT: inline methods by name, cache stores by computed key

- A method call whose callee is not known (`base.name(...)`, with no type
  table) is taken for the one function the program stores under that name
  (MethodsOfProgram: object literals, class bodies, `x.name = function`),
  when there is exactly one and it is not the name of a standard method, and
  inlined behind a check that the callee is that function
  (GuardKind::IsKnownFunction: its executable's image index, patched in at
  link time by KnownCalleeNumberReferences). In a loop's fast copy the check
  leaves for the generic copy, which makes the call, so the fast copy keeps
  no call; elsewhere the call is made in place when the check fails. Only
  in loops: elsewhere the check and the copy cost more code than a call.
- put_by_val with an atom string or symbol key stores through the VM's
  megamorphic cache, as get_by_val reads through it: an object used as a
  dictionary no longer takes a C++ call per store.
